  "sections": {
    "review": {
      "summary": "Read the owner's DvP specification v1.1 in full (sections 0-14) and the repository's DvP code, tests, configs, receipts and documents. Mapped every action item to evidence: 14 operating rules, RQ1-RQ7, definitions, the data boundary and eligibility table, datasets and reconciliation checks, v0 items, A00-A12, B00-B12, C00-C05, statistics, metrics and decision rules, T01-T40, phases 0-5, CLI contracts and modes, config and record fields, section 11 deliverables and before-completion checks, the section 12 decision chain and the section 13 caveats. Reran every stage on scratch copies (audit, reproduce-v0, reliability, development, validation from main; 2025 holdout from the frozen tree 165d140; holdout refused from main; sitstart; verify; report; registry): every receipt equals its committed version apart from code, time, run ID, byte hashes of Parquet files and fields added after a receipt was made; holdout forecasts equal within 7.1e-15 (18 values). Found: DATA_QUALITY.md and V0_REPRODUCTION.md cite an earlier audit run (021910Z, bc414a0) than their receipts (024442Z, 3a1fe11); dry-run and resume modes were never built; the project next action still says to merge PR #12, which is merged.",
      "files": [
        "docs/research/dvp/DATA_QUALITY.md",
        "docs/research/dvp/V0_REPRODUCTION.md"
      ]
    },
    "plan": {
      "summary": "1) Encode the item-to-evidence map as an executable audit, scripts/model/dvp_plan_audit.py: 'rerun' copies the frozen audit run and receipts to scratch and reruns every stage (holdout from a worktree at 165d140; the holdout's refusal from this tree) plus the model tests with JUnit results; 'check' evaluates every item's checks and writes docs/research/dvp/plan-audit-receipt.json (DONE / OPEN / FAILED per item; exit 1 on any failure). Open items (prospective 2026 scoring, owner weight, C03, league lineups, dry-run/resume) are kind 'open': their checks prove the open state is recorded, never count as done. 2) Tests (test_dvp_plan_audit.py): catalog covers every specified ID; every check defined and used; every T tag names real tests; open items never count as done; receipt comparison and forecast-difference logic; committed receipt passes, matches the catalog and the specification hash; the scope document has a row for every item. 3) Commit code first, then run the audit so the receipt names a clean commit. 4) Write PLAN_COMPLETION_SCOPE.md (every item: status, code/model logic, proof) from the receipt. 5) Fix the stale run IDs; update README, status, changelog, state.json next action; handoff.",
